 "remarks": "Tucked into a quiet corner of the complex, this charming two-bedroom, one-and-a-half-bath townhouse offers 1,260 square feet of private, move-in ready living in Stamford. The backyard faces a single-family home rather than another unit, giving it a peaceful, tucked-away feel that's rare in condo living. Hardwood floors run throughout, and the renovated kitchen features shaker cabinetry, marble countertops, and a new oven and refrigerator. The big-ticket items are already handled, with a brand-new deck, new windows, and a new storm door, so the next owner can simply move in and enjoy. The deck is a natural spot for morning coffee, grilling, or unwinding at the end of the day in a setting that feels far more private than typical townhouse living. Upstairs, two bedrooms offer generous closet space, with a washer and dryer conveniently located on the same level. A crawl space provides extra storage for seasonal items, and an existing alarm system can be activated for added peace of mind. Step outside and everyday errands are an easy walk, with a park, grocery store, CVS, bakery, and ice cream shop all nearby. Downtown Stamford's restaurants and shops are less than three miles away, and commuters can choose between the Stamford, Springdale, and Glenbrook Metro-North stations. A dedicated parking space, low HOA fees, and an association with no pet restrictions make ownership as easy as it gets.",
